From: Michal Gawronski-Kot <michal@gawronskikot.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mcp): skip server notifications when reading an SSE tool response

Local komodo_library patch on top of v0.8.5 (not upstream). Streamable-HTTP
servers may emit notifications/* frames before the JSON-RPC response;
JsonRpcResponse has all-optional fields so such a frame parsed as an empty
response and the tool call failed with "outcome unknown" (Home Assistant
ha_search, ~26s with a progress frame at ~1s).
---
--- a/crates/zeroclaw-tools/src/mcp_transport.rs
+++ b/crates/zeroclaw-tools/src/mcp_transport.rs
@@ -1914,7 +1914,24 @@
                 continue;
             }
             let json_str = extract_json_from_sse_text(trimmed);
-            if let Ok(resp) = serde_json::from_str::<JsonRpcResponse>(json_str.as_ref()) {
+            // Local patch 0003 (komodo_library): skip server-initiated frames.
+            // A server may interleave `notifications/*` (e.g. progress logging)
+            // on the same stream before the response; those parse into
+            // `JsonRpcResponse` with every field `None` because `id`, `result`
+            // and `error` are all optional, so returning the first parseable
+            // frame surfaced a bogus empty response and the tool call failed
+            // with "outcome unknown". Home Assistant's ha_search does exactly
+            // this. Keep reading until a frame carries `id`, `result` or
+            // `error`.
+            if let Ok(value) = serde_json::from_str::<serde_json::Value>(json_str.as_ref())
+                && value.get("method").is_some()
+                && value.get("id").is_none()
+            {
+                continue;
+            }
+            if let Ok(resp) = serde_json::from_str::<JsonRpcResponse>(json_str.as_ref())
+                && (resp.id.is_some() || resp.result.is_some() || resp.error.is_some())
+            {
                 return Ok(Some(resp));
             }
             continue;
